# The RAIL crate links a vendor blob and compiles one vendor C file, and both are part of the build:
#
#   blobs/efr32mg24b220/librail_efr32xg24_gcc_release.a   the radio library itself
#   vendor/rail/**                                        the headers the bindings are generated from
#   vendor/pa_auto_mode/pa_auto_mode.c                    the PA table helper the blob expects
#
# Both were excluded here, which made a clean clone fail in this crate with "vendor/pa_auto_mode/
# pa_auto_mode.c: No such file or directory" -- a file the reader has no way to obtain. The repository
# publishes the Bluetooth and NVM3 archives for the same reason: a radio crate whose inputs are missing is a
# radio crate nobody can build.
#
# They stay small enough not to matter (1.5 MB of archive, 1.2 MB of headers), and the alternative -- fetching
# the Gecko SDK inside the build -- would need a mapping from SDK layout to our vendor layout that can drift
# silently. Publishing is the honest option.
#
# Build output and generated bindings are still ignored, below.
target/
Cargo.lock
bindings.rs
